==Battleground==
*1 [[Le'noir]] spawns.
*10 [[Pigge]]s spawn after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*3 [[Helmut Krabbe]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**8 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**1 [[Le'noir]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is not very wide but has many easy peons for money, enough to summon several heavy-hitters before hitting the base. Angelic Beast Rajakong pushes very hard and without [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] this can be somewhat difficult to deal with. Bringing at least 2 [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] is advised. You generally want to stall the Le'noir and peons for cash, as Rajakong's insane pushing power can lead to funds being drained quickly.

===='''Recommended Units'''====
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]]: Thanks to his immunity to Waves, he serves as one of the best non-Uber options for wearing down Rajakong.
*[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]: Helps with stalling at the start due to its ability to freeze Le'noir, and can also freeze the second one behind the Rajakong due to how often it gets knocked back.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: In addition to being good against Rajakong's Angel typing, his high overall health makes him good for stalling the peons at the beginning.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Able to dispose of the Pigges at the start, and can deal solid damage to the rest of the enemies, particularly Rajakong and Wild Doge.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]: Practically mandatory for this stage, as it was tailor-made to beat Rajakong with its Wave immunity and great DPS against Angels/Behemoths.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Can help chip down the Le'noir at the beginning, especially if his Wave talent is maxed out, and can help against the other enemies thanks to his good bulk.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: A solid choice for regaining ground, as he will hit Rajakong almost every time due to how it is always at the front. '''It is heavily advised to wait until the first Le'noir is dead before spawning him''', as he can potentially knock the pachyderm behind the enemy base, leading to the base getting hit and Rajakong being summoned early.

